# Normalize line endings across Windows and Linux. Repo standard is LF.
# Git auto-detects text vs binary; binaries are left alone.
* text=auto eol=lf

# cmd.exe re-seeks the script by byte offset after each command, so an LF-only
# batch file can resume in the middle of a line and run the fragment. It
# depends on the byte layout, which is why some of these files work and some
# print stray errors. These two are checked out CRLF for that reason.
#
# The other .bat files in this tree are still LF and carry the same latent
# fault; `*.bat text eol=crlf` would settle it for all of them.
FRATERNITE_HD/encrypt_translations.bat text eol=crlf
FRATERNITE_HD/decrypt_translations.bat text eol=crlf
